   "he": "הַיּוֹרֵשׁ סוֹמֵךְ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: If the owner of an offering died, then «the heir» is regarded as the offering’s owner. Therefore, he «places» his «hands» on the offering and brings the accompanying libations, and he can substitute a non-sacred animal for it. Although it is prohibited to perform an act of substitution, if the owner of an offering does this, his attempt is successful to the extent that the non-sacred animal is thereby consecrated, even though the original offering also remains sacred."
  }
